  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Cyproheptadine is an antihistamine used for allergic conditions such as urticaria, angioedema and vasomotor rhinitis, and has also been used in conditions like Nelson syndrome. It is an approved drug, but it is not authorised in the European Union and is used relatively little there.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417884&quot;>Wikidata Q417884</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>cyproheptadine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>R06AX02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00434&quot;>DB00434</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/2913&quot;>2913</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:4046&quot;>4046</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q417884&quot;>Q417884</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C21H21N</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>287.406 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
